{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook, but it's so much more than that. it's a story about the cutthroat world of technology, about ambition, about friendship, and about the true cost of success.\n\nthe film follows the life of mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a young and brilliant college student who creates facebook with his friends edgar and davis. the movie takes us on a journey through the highs and lows of their relationship, from the early days of the website to the subsequent lawsuits and controversies that followed.\n\none of the standout aspects of the film is its portrayal of the characters. the actors bring to life the real-life personalities of mark, edgar, and davis, capturing their quirks, their insecurities, and their strengths. jesse eisenberg's performance as mark zuckerberg is particularly noteworthy, conveying the complexity and intensity of the character.\n\nthe film's directing is also noteworthy. david fincher's distinctive style brings a sense of tension and unease to the film, perfectly capturing the mood of the characters. the cinematography is equally impressive, capturing the cramped and claustrophobic atmosphere of the characters' college dorm rooms and the sleek, modern world of the tech industry.\n\nthe script, written by grant heslov, benj pasek, and jason reitman, is razor-sharp and witty, capturing the humor and wit of the characters. the dialogue is often hilarious, but also poignantly insightful, revealing the characters' true feelings and motivations.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally impressive, perfectly capturing the mood of the film. the music is often discordant and jarring, reflecting the tension and unease of the characters.\n\none of the most striking aspects of the film is its portrayal of the darker side of ambition. mark zuckerberg's relentless pursuit of success comes at a great cost, both personally and professionally. the film shows how the pressure to succeed can consume and destroy relationships, and how the pursuit of wealth and power can lead to a loss of integrity and compassion.\n\noverall, the social network is a brilliant film that is both entertaining and thought-provoking. it's a film that will make you laugh, cry, and think, and one that will stay with you long after the credits roll.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00035589560866355896}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680097848176956}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009609610424377024}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -2.0224790573120117}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.012613166123628616}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -1.805653691291809}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00027092601521871984}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -0.005760496947914362}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04134836047887802}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.03191991522908211}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0007838514284230769}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.03058483637869358}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.3194352686405182}, {"token": " but", "logprob": -0.5803464651107788}, {"token": " it", "logprob": -0.051235005259513855}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.19270989298820496}, {"token": " so", "logprob": -1.8627049922943115}, {"token": " much", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " more", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-06}, {"token": " than", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.05577472224831581}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.00048065552255138755}, {"token": " it", "logprob": -0.24592074751853943}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00563935749232769}, {"token": " story", "lo